diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 471732d6..d45eb006 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -326,6 +326,18 @@ Format follows [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/).
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **Vulkan, qwen36: a long first prompt took experts out of the tier for the rest of the
+  process.** Before its first prompt chunk's scratch exists, the chain kept free all the memory
+  beside an 8192-position KV mirror, so a longer first prompt's mirror took its rows past 8192
+  positions from the expert tier, which lowers its maximum and does not take them back. An Arc
+  Pro B60 with Qwen3.6-35B-A3B's 18 GiB tier, a 16K-token prompt as the first request: 78
+  experts out, that prompt 74.4 -> 88.6 s, decode 35 -> 24-30 tok/s after it (a short first
+  request kept every expert). Such a mirror now keeps free only the first chunk's scratch, the
+  tier's staging room and 256 MiB, the chunk decided before it (`q36c_mirror`), where the device
+  reports its budget (`VK_EXT_memory_budget`) and the mirror fits in the half of the free memory
+  a chunk leaves; a first mirror within 8192 positions, or one past that half, goes as before. A
+  short first request still decides its chunk after its own mirror, so a long one's can come
+  out one 256-row step bigger on the B60.
 - **`chat_template_kwargs` reaches the chat template** (`coli serve`). Many OpenAI-compatible
   clients turn a Qwen model's thinking off with `"chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking":
   false}`, and the gateway ignored the field: a Qwen3.8 request that asked for no thinking this
